00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.490
Hello friends, Doctor prasoon here. There
is no doubt you will need a health

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.030
insurance. If you don't have one, you
should definitely take a health

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.349
insurance for yourself and for your
family. But, how will you choose the right

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:17.609
and the best health insurance which is
available in India?. Which health

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:21.779
insurance plan is the right one for you?.
In this video, I am going to tell you

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:26.490
some tips which most of the health
insurance companies hide from customers.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:31.529
These are some tips which most people
overlook when they try to find the right

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:36.059
health insurance plan for themselves.
Welcome back to Dofody, Online doctor

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:55.770
consultation. So let's get started. The
first point that you should consider is,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:00.140
The network hospitals Which the
insurance company has a tie-up with.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.809
Instead of going behind insurance
companies and searching for the best

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.460
insurance companies, what you should be
doing is, find out the best Hospital in

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.770
your area. Select that hospital
which has the most number of specialty

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.030
doctors, which has all the specialty
departments in it, which has all the

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:23.400
facilities, and then ask the hospital
with which insurance company they have a

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.140
cashless claim tie-up. They will give you a
list of insurance companies with whom

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:33.420
they have a direct tie up and from that
list usually selecting your insurance

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.560
company. You can double-check that by
visiting the insurance company's website,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.390
selecting your state, then your district.
You can find the list of hospitals with

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:48.090
which the insurance company has a tie-up.These group of hospitals with which the

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.689
insurance company have a direct tie-up, these are called as a network

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:56.399
hospitals, who sometimes called as
connected hospitals. The advantages of a

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:02.009
cashless claim is huge, particularly when
an emergency condition such as a surgery

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:07.439
pops up in your life. You don't have to
go run around searching for money,

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:12.390
arranging the money to do the surgery or
to pay off the hospital bills.Your

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.349
insurance company will be
directly paying the hospital, and you

00:02:16.349 --> 00:02:20.520
will not have to take a single penny out
of your pocket. The second point to note

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:27.690
is the maximum room rent the insurance
company lays down in its insurance plan.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:33.390
Most of the insurance companies have a
maximum capping of the room rent which

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:40.170
the customer can avail. For example, if an
insurance plan offers capping of 2500

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.750
rupees as the maximum room rent per day,
and if you are opting an air-conditioned

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:51.930
room a single room with a room rent of
3500 per day. Normally what we think is

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:56.250
that we will have to pay a difference of
1000 rupees every day for the period of

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.870
hospital admission. But, that is far from
the truth. Actually what happens is that

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:06.330
there is something which is called as
proportionate direction. I will explain

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:11.489
what a proportionate deduction is. Based
on the hospital fee structure, the

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:16.350
service charges, the hospital fees, the
doctors fee, the nurses fee, and everything

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:20.880
will be different. For the patients who
are admitted in a general ward, a shared

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.220
room and in a standard AC room and even
in a deluxe room. All these charges will

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.299
be different. So if you are thinking that
you will have to just pay a 1000 rupees

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:36.359
difference? you are wrong! Because in the
AC standard room that you are chosen, the

00:03:36.359 --> 00:03:40.260
doctors fee will be higher, the nursing
fee will be higher, the service charges

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.160
will be higher, the procedure charges
will be higher, and you will have to

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.410
shell out the extra difference from your
pocket, and this difference the insurance

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.250
company is not going to cover this
difference and that is called a

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:57.450
proportionate deduction. So, Always keep
in mind to choose the right room. If you

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.519
already have a policy or else if you are
trying to find a new health insurance

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:06.840
policy for yourself, try to find out
those insurance companies which does not

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.269
restrict on the daily room rent, or go
for those companies which offers a

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:17.100
single standard air-conditioned room
without putting a maximum limit on the

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.870
maximum room rent that you can avail
every day. The third thing that you

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.440
should be looking for is something
called as the waiting period or the

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.350
freezing period.
Most of the insurance companies have a

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:34.110
waiting period of one year or two years.
That means, after taking the policy you

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.920
will not be able to make any claims
within the waiting period. Most of the

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.660
standard companies have a waiting period
of one to two years, and it will

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.640
be different for different conditions.
For example, the pregnancy charges the

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.170
delivery charges will not be covered in
the waiting period, a surgery will not be

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:55.650
covered in the waiting period, and all
these details will be given finally

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.040
printed in the terms and conditions
which you are obviously not going to

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:03.180
read completely. So, always inquire these
things before you finally make a

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:08.610
decision to go with a certain specific
health insurance policy. Point number

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.750
four is revealing your pre-existing
medical conditions or surgical

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.370
conditions. Now what most people tend to
do is that they hide whatever medical

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:21.270
conditions they had when they are taking
or filling up the form for the health

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:24.870
insurance policy. You should never do
this, because the health insurance

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:29.790
company is anyway going to find out your
previous medical history when you raise

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:34.500
a claim, and when they find out that you
had a previous existing medical

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:43.860
condition for which you are raising the
claim right now. They are going to deny it, 
 They are going to reject it. So
instead of keep on pressing the next

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.580
button menu filling of the online form
or when you are filling of the form

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:52.920
offline in a paper, always reveal your
medical conditions whether it be a high

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.440
blood pressure, diabetes, a heart
condition, a kidney problem, liver disease,

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.740
whatever that you are suffering from
that you have been diagnosed earlier.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:06.570
Reveal it, write it down, and let them
know that you have these conditions.The

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:11.790
premium will be a bit higher. But you can
be assured that these companies are

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:16.920
going to settle your claim if god forbid
something bad happens to you, and when

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.690
you are trying to raise a claim at the
time of an emergency, you are policy your

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:27.870
claim doesn't get rejected. The next
point is choosing a insurance policy

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:33.110
which covers pre hospitalization as well
as post hospitalization expenses. A

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:38.220
standard health insurance company is
going to cover anywhere between one

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:42.619
month pre-hospitalization
and 90 days post-hospitalization.

00:06:42.619 --> 00:06:48.899
Some companies even go up to 120 days of
post-hospitalization. That means all the

00:06:48.899 --> 00:06:52.860
medical expenses all the expenses for
the purchase of medicines after

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.899
discharge, your ambulance fees, all the
tests you've done before you got

00:06:57.899 --> 00:07:00.989
admitted in the hospital, all these
things are going to be covered under

00:07:00.989 --> 00:07:05.309
these policies. So make sure that you
choose a health insurance policy which

00:07:05.309 --> 00:07:08.849
covers at least one month pre
hospitalization and 90 days post

00:07:08.849 --> 00:07:13.319
hospitalization expenses. If you don't
have a cashless claim, you should also

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:17.519
keep in mind to keep all the bills
reports the doctor's prescription

00:07:17.519 --> 00:07:21.539
everything in original and duplicate and
you should apply for the claim within

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:26.249
one month of discharge. Next point is
something related to third party

00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:29.989
administrators. Now there are some
insurance companies which do not have a

00:07:29.989 --> 00:07:34.860
claim settlement team of their own. So
what they do is that they depend on

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:39.360
certain other companies which are called
as third party administrators to inquire

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.380
into the claim.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.399
Now these third party
administrators goes into the hospital checks whether the patient has got
admitted or not ,what all tests has been

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:51.029
done, what are the procedures the patient
has underwent. Now that's the job of

00:07:51.029 --> 00:07:55.619
these third party administrators. Now the
problem with third party administrators

00:07:55.619 --> 00:08:01.139
is that they act as a link between
yourself, your Hospital, and your

00:08:01.139 --> 00:08:06.240
insurance company. So if you are raising
a cashless claim, it is going to be

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:11.489
delayed When a third party administrator
has got involved. Your discharge will be

00:08:11.489 --> 00:08:15.599
getting delayed. You will have to shell
out some money from your pocket and the

00:08:15.599 --> 00:08:20.399
overall experience is not going to be so
good when compared to another health

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:25.739
insurance company which has its own
claim settlement team. Now this has

00:08:25.739 --> 00:08:29.129
happened to me when my father got
admitted for an angioplasty procedure.

00:08:29.129 --> 00:08:34.050
Our hospital stay was not a pleasant one,
there was a third party administrator

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:39.689
involved in our case, and the discharge
process got delayed. Even though we had a

00:08:39.689 --> 00:08:43.529
cashless claim the whole process got
delayed because of the involvement of

00:08:43.529 --> 00:08:47.790
the third party administrator. So what I
recommend is that you should always go

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:53.069
with a health insurance company which
has its own or in-house claim settlement

00:08:53.069 --> 00:08:54.560
team. Now there

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.950
are some other special plans

00:08:55.950 --> 00:09:01.470
such as the cancer care plan and there
are other topper plans, super topper

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:06.540
plans, which you can get in addition to
the policies that you're holding. The

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:11.760
topper plans and the superb topper plans
will cover the amount in extra of what

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.840
the sum assured you have been guaranteed.
If you have hospital expenses in any

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:21.720
process the amount which your policy has
assured then the super topper plans was

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:26.730
going to help you out. The super topper
plans will also come at a low premium. So

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.140
you should always consider buying a
super topper plan if you're some assured

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:36.270
is on the lower side below two lakhs or
below three lakhs, and you should always

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:42.000
go for special plans such as cancer care
plans if someone in your family has

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.650
already been diagnosed with cancer, if
you are at a higher risk of developing a

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:51.210
cancer in the future. Now another miss
concept which most people think is that,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:56.220
if you disclose about the insurance at
the time of admission, the doctors are

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:00.120
going to over treat you they are going
to do unwanted procedures, unwanted

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:04.650
surgeries and all. Now this is actually a
misunderstanding, because all the

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.700
insurance companies have their own team
of medical doctors and these doctors are

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:13.350
going to check in with your treating
doctor whether the procedure was

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:17.580
actually required or not, whether the
diagnostic test your doctor has written

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.080
was actually required or not, and for
that reason the doctor who is treating

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:27.000
you will be on the cautious side he is
not going to write unwanted tests or do

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:30.900
any unwanted procedures. So, this is
actually a convenience. You can actually

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:36.420
have a peace of mind because of the fact
that you don't have to spend any money

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:41.040
when it comes to a hospital and
admission, when it comes to an emergency

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.050
hospital procedure, or a surgery. So if
you haven't subscribed to a health

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:50.640
insurance policy, please do it right now.
It is an absolute necessary in this age

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:55.260
and if you already have a health
insurance policy please let me know

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:58.830
which insurance policy you are using
whether you are raised any claims and

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:04.290
how was your experience after raising an
insurance claim. So I hope you really

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:07.620
liked this video, if you haven't
subscribe to our Channel,

